body:
$P =$ {prime numbers less than 20}

$Q =$ {odd numbers less than 10}

Find $P \cap Q$.

answer:
**(a)(ii)** $AB$ is horizontal and $AC$ is vertical, so the triangle is right-angled at $A$.

**(b)** $A_1\left(-1, 1\frac{1}{2}\right)$, $B_1\left(-4, 1\frac{1}{2}\right)$, $C_1(-1, 4)$

**(c)** $A_2\left(-1, -1\frac{1}{2}\right)$, $B_2\left(-4, -1\frac{1}{2}\right)$, $C_2(-1, -4)$

**(d)** Each point keeps its $x$-coordinate and its $y$-coordinate changes sign.

> [!answer]
> **(a)(ii)** {{green:right-angled}}
>
> **(b)** {{green:$A_1\left(-1, 1\frac{1}{2}\right)$, $B_1\left(-4, 1\frac{1}{2}\right)$, $C_1(-1, 4)$}}
>
> **(c)** {{green:$A_2\left(-1, -1\frac{1}{2}\right)$, $B_2\left(-4, -1\frac{1}{2}\right)$, $C_2(-1, -4)$}}
>
> **(d)** {{green:a reflection in the $x$-axis}}
